T1  - Microalbuminuria: is it a valid predictor of cardiovascular risk?.
DO  - https://dx.doi.org/10.3949/ccjm.70.3.255
A1  - Tagle, Rodrigo
A1  - Acevedo, Monica
A1  - Vidt, Donald G
Y1  - 2003//
N2  - Microalbuminuria strongly predicts cardiovascular morbidity and mortality, clinical nephropathy, and progression of renal disease in high-risk populations. We recommend screening patients with type 2 diabetes, older patients with type 1 diabetes, and older patients with stage 2 hypertension or higher (ie, > or = 160/100 mm Hg).
